+## Repository context
+
+This repository is a maintained derivative of the upstream [DeepSeek Harness repository](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness). It adds these product capabilities:
+
+- **Workspace-isolated execution** — The `workspace-isolated` sandbox limits model-facing filesystem operations to the session workspace. On Linux, confined shell and terminal processes require Bubblewrap, can read only the workspace plus configured runtime paths, write only inside the workspace, and cannot request a wider sandbox retry. See the [sandbox details](docs/subsystems/sandbox.md).
+- **PDF-aware `web_fetch`** — HTTP fetch accepts text-bearing PDFs, extracts embedded text into ordered page entries, preserves page numbers, and enforces the existing byte and character limits plus a PDF page cap. Malformed, encrypted, and image-only PDFs fail explicitly; OCR is not included. See the [web fetch details](packages/web/web-fetch-http/README.md).
+
+### Preferred JobBench profile
+
+The strongest observed GPT-5.6 Luna JobBench performance used the OpenAI Responses API at `http://127.0.0.1:8003/v1`, `high` reasoning, a 262,144-token context window, a 32,768-token output cap, Exa web search, HTTP fetch, one task at a time, and a 3,600-second task limit. Each task ran with a private DSH home, a fresh task workspace, `approval: never`, and the `workspace-write` policy.
+
+This profile selected the Linux Landlock backend and did not use Bubblewrap or the Bubblewrap-only `workspace-isolated` mode. Landlock kept writes inside the task workspace while preserving the host reads required by the JobBench toolchain. Treat the result as evidence for the complete profile rather than a controlled Landlock-versus-Bubblewrap comparison, and use it only when host-read isolation is not required.
+
 ## Developer preview
 
 DeepSeek Harness is in _developer preview_ and iterating rapidly. **THERE WILL BE COMPATIBILITY-BREAKING CHANGES.**
